1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,600
This is Press.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,720
One phone keeps score for the whole

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:10,100
group — skins, Nassau, Wolf, the lot

4
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:12,800
— and it does the math while

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,560
you play.

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,700
No account, no app store, nothing to

7
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,300
install.

8
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:21,520
Here's a full round in four minutes.

9
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:27,280
Start New Round, and type everyone in.

10
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,400
The handicap goes in the box beside

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,420
the name — that's what every net

12
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:33,960
score in the round comes off.

13
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:37,140
Press remembers your regular crew, so next

14
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:38,860
week this is one tap.

15
00:00:40,547 --> 00:00:41,147
Open Course.

16
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:43,807
Search for it and Press pulls in

17
00:00:43,807 --> 00:00:46,007
the pars and the stroke indexes, or

18
00:00:46,007 --> 00:00:47,247
load one you saved earlier.

19
00:00:48,347 --> 00:00:50,067
Check them against the real card once.

20
00:00:51,007 --> 00:00:53,547
Every stroke anybody gets comes off these

21
00:00:53,547 --> 00:00:54,387
eighteen numbers.

22
00:00:56,147 --> 00:00:58,007
Games is where the money starts.

23
00:00:59,247 --> 00:01:01,127
Tap what you're playing.

24
00:01:01,127 --> 00:01:04,187
Every format carries its own rules behind

25
00:01:04,187 --> 00:01:08,047
the little i — so when somebody

26
00:01:08,047 --> 00:01:09,847
at the table has never played Wolf,

27
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:11,807
you don't have to be the one

28
00:01:11,807 --> 00:01:12,567
who explains it.

29
00:01:14,114 --> 00:01:15,154
The full list:

30
00:01:15,914 --> 00:01:19,254
stroke play, match play — singles or

31
00:01:19,254 --> 00:01:23,274
two-man best ball — skins, Stableford, Wolf,

32
00:01:23,734 --> 00:01:26,914
Vegas with the birdie flip, Quota, Nassau

33
00:01:26,914 --> 00:01:29,914
with presses, and a Thursday-night league format.

34
00:01:31,034 --> 00:01:33,034
Net runs through all of it:

35
00:01:33,734 --> 00:01:36,034
one stroke per hole down the stroke

36
00:01:36,034 --> 00:01:38,634
index, and a second on the hardest

37
00:01:38,634 --> 00:01:41,194
holes when somebody's playing off more than

38
00:01:41,194 --> 00:01:41,794
eighteen.

39
00:01:43,314 --> 00:01:45,434
Money sets the stake per game.

40
00:01:46,274 --> 00:01:47,934
Five a skin, twenty on the Nassau.

41
00:01:47,934 --> 00:01:51,154
Leave it blank and you're playing for

42
00:01:51,154 --> 00:01:53,634
nothing — and you can change it

43
00:01:53,634 --> 00:01:54,494
mid-round from the Board.

44
00:01:56,184 --> 00:01:59,364
Start Round, and this is where you

45
00:01:59,364 --> 00:02:01,784
live for the next four hours.

46
00:02:02,944 --> 00:02:06,844
Hole number, par, one row per player.

47
00:02:07,964 --> 00:02:08,584
Tap the score.

48
00:02:09,764 --> 00:02:11,444
Par is the chip in the middle,

49
00:02:12,104 --> 00:02:14,824
and the dots beside a name are

50
00:02:14,824 --> 00:02:16,524
the strokes they're getting on this hole.

51
00:02:18,184 --> 00:02:20,344
The line at the top is the

52
00:02:20,344 --> 00:02:23,004
money, live, all round.

53
00:02:24,064 --> 00:02:26,064
Close out a hole and it tells

54
00:02:26,064 --> 00:02:29,084
you exactly what just changed hands, and

55
00:02:29,084 --> 00:02:30,064
who it came from.

56
00:02:31,454 --> 00:02:35,154
Greenies, sandies, barkies — claim them on

57
00:02:35,154 --> 00:02:36,934
the hole and they land on the

58
00:02:37,614 --> 00:02:38,934
card, priced.

59
00:02:38,934 --> 00:02:41,204
Wolf picks its partner right here, before

60
00:02:41,214 --> 00:02:42,014
anybody's hit.

61
00:02:42,894 --> 00:02:43,934
Nassau presses too:

62
00:02:44,674 --> 00:02:46,574
take one by hand, or set it

63
00:02:46,574 --> 00:02:48,634
to press automatically when a side goes

64
00:02:48,634 --> 00:02:49,314
two down.

65
00:02:50,934 --> 00:02:53,074
The Board tab is every game at

66
00:02:53,074 --> 00:02:54,994
once — who's up in the match,

67
00:02:55,214 --> 00:02:57,914
who's holding skins, where the money actually

68
00:02:57,914 --> 00:02:58,514
sits.

69
00:02:59,374 --> 00:03:01,174
Somebody gave you the wrong handicap on

70
00:03:01,174 --> 00:03:01,774
the first tee?

71
00:03:02,394 --> 00:03:04,614
Fix it here, and every board behind

72
00:03:04,614 --> 00:03:05,754
it recalculates.

73
00:03:07,401 --> 00:03:09,781
Card is the whole scorecard, eighteen across.

74
00:03:09,781 --> 00:03:13,161
Tap a number to fix it, tap

75
00:03:13,161 --> 00:03:14,881
a hole to jump straight back to

76
00:03:14,881 --> 00:03:15,481
it.

77
00:03:16,581 --> 00:03:19,041
Finish the round and Press settles it.

78
00:03:19,041 --> 00:03:22,561
Winner up top, then the superlatives —

79
00:03:22,561 --> 00:03:26,421
Shot of the Day, The Snowman, The

80
00:03:26,421 --> 00:03:32,001
ATM, Sandbagger — and each one cites

81
00:03:32,001 --> 00:03:34,051
the number it's based on, so the

82
00:03:34,061 --> 00:03:37,661
argument is short.

83
00:03:39,541 --> 00:03:41,841
Then the bit that normally takes ten

84
00:03:41,841 --> 00:03:42,981
minutes in the car park.

85
00:03:43,821 --> 00:03:46,581
Press resolves the whole group into the

86
00:03:46,581 --> 00:03:50,161
fewest payments that settle it.

87
00:03:50,161 --> 00:03:51,981
Three people pay, not twelve.

88
00:03:53,681 --> 00:03:55,921
Share gives you the scoreboard as an

89
00:03:55,921 --> 00:03:58,301
image, the full card as an image,

90
00:03:58,721 --> 00:04:00,761
or plain text for the group chat.

91
00:04:02,491 --> 00:04:04,431
And underneath, the round itself.

92
00:04:05,491 --> 00:04:07,611
The whole thing is packed into the

93
00:04:07,611 --> 00:04:10,361
link — point another phone's camera at

94
00:04:10,371 --> 00:04:11,791
the code and it opens in their

95
00:04:11,791 --> 00:04:12,631
copy of Press.

96
00:04:13,591 --> 00:04:14,511
Nothing is uploaded.

97
00:04:15,571 --> 00:04:16,951
No server ever sees it.

98
00:04:20,191 --> 00:04:23,131
On their phone it arrives held —

99
00:04:23,131 --> 00:04:25,311
sent to you, not saved — until

100
00:04:25,311 --> 00:04:27,131
they tap Keep it.

101
00:04:27,531 --> 00:04:29,391
Mid-round, the same link hands the card

102
00:04:29,691 --> 00:04:31,671
over and they carry on scoring from

103
00:04:31,671 --> 00:04:33,111
where you stopped.

104
00:04:33,111 --> 00:04:35,011
And if you both end up keeping

105
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:37,691
score, Press puts the two cards side

106
00:04:37,691 --> 00:04:40,871
by side and asks which one is

107
00:04:40,871 --> 00:04:41,471
real.

108
00:04:42,871 --> 00:04:44,011
Which brings us to the thing that

109
00:04:44,011 --> 00:04:45,771
actually matters out on the course.

110
00:04:46,591 --> 00:04:47,191
Watch:

111
00:04:47,531 --> 00:04:48,991
I'm killing the network completely.

112
00:04:49,891 --> 00:04:50,491
Reload.

113
00:04:51,111 --> 00:04:52,611
Still there, still scoring.

114
00:04:53,791 --> 00:04:56,331
Every round, every saved course, every bit

115
00:04:56,331 --> 00:04:58,151
of history lives on your phone.

116
00:04:58,151 --> 00:05:01,651
That's the privacy story too — there's

117
00:05:01,651 --> 00:05:03,691
no account to make, and nothing to

118
00:05:03,691 --> 00:05:04,291
leak.

119
00:05:05,541 --> 00:05:07,121
Add it to your home screen and

120
00:05:07,121 --> 00:05:09,101
it opens like anything else on your

121
00:05:09,801 --> 00:05:09,931
phone.

122
00:05:09,941 --> 00:05:14,181
It's free, it's at pressgolf.netlify.app, and the

123
00:05:14,181 --> 00:05:14,921
link's in the description.

124
00:05:14,921 --> 00:05:17,161
Now go take their money.
